          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Detener al final del libro"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Stop at the end of this heading" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the sleep timer sheet's End of heading button, which sets a timer that stops where the heading playing ends.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Detener al final de este encabezado"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Stopped. Back at %@." : {
      "comment" : "Said as the audio editor's Stop goes back to where playing began. %@ is that time in words."
    },
    "Stops playing, and goes back to where playing began." : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the audio editor's Stop button."
    },
    "Takes %lld to %lld minutes." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the sleep timer sheet's custom minutes field on the iPhone: the fewest and most minutes it takes. %1$lld is the fewest (1); %2$lld the most (480).",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Takes %1$lld to %2$lld minutes."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Admite de %1$lld a %2$lld minutos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Takes %lld to %lld minutes. Return sets the timer and plays the book." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the sleep timer sheet's custom minutes field on the Mac: the fewest and most minutes it takes, and what the Return key does there. %1$lld is the fewest (1); %2$lld the most (480). Return is the name of the key.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Takes %1$lld to %2$lld minutes. Return sets the timer and plays the book."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Admite de %1$lld a %2$lld minutos. Retorno programa el temporizador y reproduce el libro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Takes each finished book off the list when its window moves on or closes. Books finished before you turn it on stay." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Reading List's Remove books when finished checkbox.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Quita de la lista cada libro terminado cuando su ventana pasa a otro libro o se cierra. Los libros terminados antes de activarlo se quedan."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Takes the selected books off the reading list. They stay in the library." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Library's edit-mode bar button Remove from Reading List.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Quita los libros seleccionados de la lista de lectura. Siguen en la biblioteca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth closed while opening %@, so it wasn't reopened." : {
      "comment" : "Announced at launch after the app closed while it was opening a book. %@ is the book's title, which is not opened again."
    },
    "TextMouth doesn't read chapter markers back from %@ files, so this book won't list its %lld chapter markers once saved." : {
      "comment" : "Said when a save writes the book's file in a format whose chapter markers TextMouth writes but never reads back as the book's chapters. %1$@ is the format's name, such as \"CAF\", and %2$lld the number of chapter markers.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth doesn't read chapter markers back from %@ files, so this book won't list its chapter marker once saved."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth doesn't read chapter markers back from %@ files, so this book won't list its %lld chapter markers once saved."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is not downloading right now." : {
      "comment" : "Why the download of a feed's next episode did not start: the app is quitting or the feed is being deleted. Said after \"The next episode could not be downloaded, so playback stopped.\"",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no está descargando en este momento."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is quitting and the book's audio doesn't hold these edits yet. Discard undoes them; next time you edit this book, Redo brings them back until you make another edit. Cancel keeps TextMouth open." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the question about the audio editor's unsaved edits asked as TextMouth quits: what Discard and Cancel do."
    },
    "TextMouth's own filters don't include “%@”. They are %@; with ffmpeg installed, every filter it has works." : {
      "comment" : "Problem said of a filter TextMouth doesn't run itself. %1$@ is the filter's name as typed, and %2$@ the list of the filters TextMouth does run, such as \"a, b, and c\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth's own filters don't include “%1$@”. They are %2$@; with ffmpeg installed, every filter it has works."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth's own filters run this chain." : {
      "comment" : "Shown under a filter preset's chain field: every filter in it is one TextMouth runs itself."
    },
    "TextMouth's own loudnorm normalizes with one gain, so it takes only true" : {
      "comment" : "What the loudnorm filter's linear option accepts, said at the end of a refusal such as \"The loudnorm filter's linear can't be “false”: <this>.\" Written without its full stop."
    },
    "That's after the end of the audio, at %@." : {
      "comment" : "Said when a time typed into the audio editor's Go to Time lies past the end. %@ is the audio's length in words."
    },
    "The %@ filter has no option “%@” here. Its options are %@." : {
      "comment" : "Problem said of an option a filter doesn't take. %1$@ is the filter's name, %2$@ the option as typed, and %3$@ the list of the options it takes.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The %1$@ filter has no option “%2$@” here. Its options are %3$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The %@ filter needs its %@: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Problem said when a filter lacks an option it needs. %1$@ is the filter's name, %2$@ the option's name, and %3$@ what the option takes, a clause such as \"give a time such as 2.5\", written without its full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The %1$@ filter needs its %2$@: %3$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The %@ filter was given more values than it has options; give them as key=value." : {
      "comment" : "Problem said when a filter is given more values than it has options. %@ is the filter's name. \"key=value\" is filter syntax and stays as it is."
    },
    "The %@ filter's %@ can't be “%@”: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Problem said of a value a filter's option can't take. %1$@ is the filter's name, %2$@ the option's name, %3$@ the value as typed, and %4$@ what the option takes, a clause such as \"give a number from 0 to 1\", written without its full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The %1$@ filter's %2$@ can't be “%3$@”: %4$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The %lld markers are deleted, and Redo doesn't bring them back." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the audio editor's Revert to Original confirmation: how many markers it deletes. %lld is the number of markers.",
      "localizations" : {
