    "The edit history couldn't be read. A copy was kept in the book's package." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the book's saved edit history can't be read. A copy of the unreadable file was kept in the book's package."
    },
    "The edit history is only in the cloud, not on this Mac yet." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the audio editor can't open a book: its edit history is only in the cloud. A second sentence says to try again once the book has downloaded."
    },
    "The edit history names a file outside the book, so it isn't used." : {
      "comment" : "Said when an audio edit can't proceed: the book's saved edit history points at a file outside the book's own package."
    },
    "The edit history of %@ couldn't be read." : {
      "comment" : "Question asked when a book's saved audio edit history can't be read. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "The edited audio couldn't be written." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the edited audio could not be written, whatever the technical reason, which goes to the debug log."
    },
    "The edits couldn't be saved." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the audio editor's save fails. A sentence giving the reason follows."
    },
    "The filter chain is empty." : {
      "comment" : "Problem said when a filter chain is typed as nothing at all, in the audio editor's Apply Filter and the filter presets."
    },
    "The filter presets are reset to the defaults." : {
      "comment" : "Said as every filter preset is put back to TextMouth's premade ones."
    },
    "The library isn't available, so the filter presets can't be saved." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the filter presets can't be saved because the library's data folder can't be used."
    },
    "The microphone Punch In records from. TextMouth remembers it, apart from macOS's input." : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the audio editor's microphone pop-up. \"Record window\" is TextMouth's window that records audio."
    },
    "The next article could not be downloaded, so playback stopped. %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver announcement when the download of a feed's next article failed. %@ is the download's own sentence saying why.",
      "localizations" : {
